# Keep the HOST's files out of the image.
#
# The Dockerfile runs `npm install` and then `COPY . .` — so without this file,
# a node_modules folder sitting in this directory gets copied straight over the
# one the container just installed. The image then tries to run macOS binaries
# on Alpine Linux, and `vite build` dies inside its own config loader with an
# error that says nothing about any of this.
#
# It only bites people who have run npm locally, which is why it can sit here
# unnoticed: a fresh clone (a base station, CI) has no node_modules to leak.
node_modules
dist

# Never bake local secrets or machine state into an image.
.env
.env.*
*.log
npm-debug.log*

# Not needed to build the app.
.git
.gitignore
coverage
